# ==============================================================================
# dav1d-native-tools/.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# LINE 1 IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore is the standard Visual Studio / .NET one. It
# ignores directory names that also occur inside the vendored dav1d source tree:
#
#     [Aa][Rr][Mm]/      -> dav1d/src/arm/        (all the NEON assembly)
#     [Aa][Rr][Mm]64/    -> dav1d/src/arm/64/
#     [Oo]ut/  [Ll]og/  [Rr]elease/  [Dd]ebug/  bld/  [Oo]bj/ ...
#
# Without the "!*" below, those folders would be silently left out of every
# commit, and the vendored snapshot would not build for the next person who
# cloned this repository. A nested .gitignore takes precedence over the ones
# above it, so re-including everything here and then re-ignoring only what this
# folder genuinely produces is the correct fix - and it keeps the root
# .gitignore untouched.
#
# Verify at any time with:
#     git check-ignore -v dav1d-native-tools/dav1d/src/arm/64/mc.S
#         -> should print nothing (i.e. the file is NOT ignored)
# ==============================================================================

# Re-include everything under this folder, overriding the root .gitignore.
!*
!*/

# --- what this folder really does produce, and must not commit ---------------

# Built native libraries, unstripped copies, staged archives, SHA256SUMS. ONE
# tree, shared by all three platform builds, so all seven RIDs land side by side.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH MATTERS. Without it this pattern would match ANY directory
# named "output" at any depth - including dav1d/tools/output/, which holds the
# vendored muxer sources (md5.c, y4m2.c, yuv.c) that the conformance gate's CLI
# is built from. That mistake was made and caught here on 2026-08-28: git
# reported the vendored folder as ignored, which would have shipped a snapshot
# that cannot build.
# NOTE THE TRAILING /* RATHER THAN A BARE /output/. A directory that is itself
# excluded is never descended into, so a later "!" rule can NEVER re-include a
# file inside it - "/output/" plus "!/output/README.txt" silently ignored the
# README too, which is exactly why that placeholder was missing from the
# repository until 2026-08-29. Excluding the CONTENTS instead leaves the
# directory itself visible, and the negation below then works.
/output/*

# ...except the placeholder README that explains what goes there.
!/output/README.txt

# Local scratch that the scripts may leave behind.
*.tmp
*.log
build-scratch/

# Finder droppings. Needed explicitly: the "!*" above re-includes everything
# under this folder and so overrides any .DS_Store rule inherited from the root
# or from a user's global gitignore. Without this line, building on a Mac leaves
# .DS_Store files that show up as untracked and get swept into a "git add -A".
.DS_Store
